25:T518,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Jeddah a Miqat for Umrah?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Jeddah lies inside the Miqat boundary, so it is not a Miqat. If you intend Umrah you must be in Ihram before crossing the Miqat — usually announced on your flight before landing in Jeddah."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where do I enter Ihram if I arrive at Jeddah airport?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Normally on the aircraft, when the crew announces the Miqat. If you arrive without Ihram, the relevant land Miqat is Al-Juhfah (near Rabigh), and a taxi can take you there before heading to Makkah."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can a taxi stop at the Miqat on the way to Makkah?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. On the Jeddah Airport to Makkah transfer, tell the driver in advance and they will stop at the Miqat so you can change into Ihram and pray before continuing to Makkah."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What if I forgot to enter Ihram before the Miqat?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Rulings vary, so consult a scholar. Many pilgrims travel out to the nearest Miqat (Al-Juhfah for the Jeddah direction) to enter Ihram there to avoid any shortfall before performing Umrah."}}]}1a:["$","div",null,{"className":"min-h-screen bg-[#FAFAF7] text-[#1C1C1C] pb-24","children":[[["$","script","0",{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"Article\",\"headline\":\"Miqat & Ihram When Arriving via Jeddah (Step-by-Step)\",\"description\":\"Where and when to enter Ihram if you arrive in Jeddah for Umrah — the on-board Miqat announcement, Al-Juhfah (Rabigh), and exactly what to do if you land without Ihram.\",\"url\":\"https://taxisaudiarabia.com/guides/miqat-jeddah-makkah\",\"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https://taxisaudiarabia.com/guides/miqat-jeddah-makkah\"},\"author\":{\